#!/bin/bash
gh issue create --title "Perf: severe slowdown and lost key events when typing in multi-line textfields" --body "When typing in a textarea, especially as it grows, the browser experiences severe performance degradation (down to a crawl) and starts dropping keyboard events. Likely due to massive re-allocations in the text handling or layout loop backing up WaitNextEvent."
gh issue create --title "Cache: navigating to a previously visited page after login shows cached logged-out version" --body "If a page is visited before logging in, and then visited again after login, the cache is not invalidated and the logged-out version is shown until the user manually reloads."
gh issue create --title "Chrome: Add 'Select All' (Cmd+A) to Edit menu" --body "The Edit menu currently lacks a 'Select All' command (Cmd+A)."
gh issue create --title "Chrome: Scrollbar dragging via TrackControl does not update view in real-time" --body "Dragging the scrollbar thumb only updates the viewport when the mouse is released because TrackControl is invoked without a live action procedure."
gh issue create --title "Chrome: Text selection drag outside textarea bounds does not auto-scroll" --body "Dragging the mouse to select text and moving outside the bounds of the textfield does not auto-scroll the control, and visual feedback is missing until release."
gh issue create --title "Chrome: 'Copy' command causes textfield scroll position to jump to caret" --body "Issuing a 'Copy' command on selected text in a multi-line textfield inadvertently causes the scroll position to jump to wherever the text cursor (caret) is located."
gh issue create --title "Clipboard: copying text uses UNIX LF instead of Mac OS CR" --body "When copying text from a multi-line textfield, the clipboard receives text with UNIX line endings (\`\\n\`) instead of Mac OS 9 carriage returns (\`\\r\`), resulting in square characters when pasted into other Mac applications."
gh issue create --title "Build: MacSurf.r is missing 'vers' resource, Get Info shows N/A" --body "The MacSurf.r resource file lacks a \`vers\` resource, which causes the Finder's Get Info window to display 'N/A' for the application version."
gh issue create --title "Build: Access Paths.xml uses absolute paths instead of {Project}-relative paths" --body "The exported Access Paths.xml contains absolute paths (\`Back40:Desktop Folder:patrick:...\`), which breaks importing the project on other machines unless the directory structure is exactly mirrored."
